{title: Live in Tents All Your Days}
{subtitle: Jeremiah 35:6–10; 35:1–5; 35:14–16; 35:13–17; 35:18–19}
{key: C}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [F] | [Am] |
| [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Go to the house of the Rechabites [F]now
[Am]Bring them into the chamber [G]here
[C]Set before them bowls full of [F]wine
[Am]And say to [G]them, drink some [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
We drink no [Am]wine, our father [C]said
You and your [Am]children [G]never [F]will
No houses [Am]built, no seed sown [C]down
No [Dm7]vineyards planted or [Gsus4]owned
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Live in tents [G]all your [Am]days
So that [F]you [G]may live [C]long
[F]Obeying [G]the voice of [Am]the father
[F]Keeping the com[G]mand [C]strong [F][C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We have obeyed the voice of [F]Jonadab
[Am]In everything he commanded [G]us
[C]To drink no wine all [F]our days
[Am]Neither wives [G]nor sons nor [C]daughters
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Live in tents [G]all your [Am]days
So that [F]you [G]may live [C]long
[F]Obeying [G]the voice of [Am]the father
[F]Keeping the com[G]mand [C]strong [G/B]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Am]But I [G]have spoken to you a[F]gain
[Am]And you [G]have not listened to [F]me
[Am]You [G]would not incline your [F]ear
To the [C]words I sent [G]down
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[C]Jonadab [G]son of Rec[Am]hab
Will [F]never lack [G]a descen[C]dant
To [F]stand before [G]me for[Am]ever
[F]Faithful [G]to the [C]end
{end_of_verse}

